<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) / Chindapol et al. (2013) Scleractinian coral calice septal insertion & advection-diffusion morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 51.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py` (consensus score 52.4/100). Implements the basic Milne-Edwards & Haime (1848) hexameral septal doubling sequence N_hex(k) = 6 * 2^(k-1) and decreasing cycle reach alpha_k in 2D, but omits Kunth's Law (1869) Paleozoic Rugosa serial 4-fossula insertion (N_rugosa(m) = 6 + 4m) as an evolutionary comparison/negative control, omits Chindapol et al. (2013) Péclet-number advection-diffusion boundary-layer symmetry breaking (Pe sweep from 0 to 36), lacks automated CV segmentation of the vendored Caryophyllia quadragenaria calice specimen, and lacks runtime SHA-256 dataset verification. Overall 51.8/100 (faithfulness 49.5, reproducibility 57.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 55, Morphological realism / specimen match 46, Parameter expressivity 48, Morphometric validation 49, Source and data traceability 62, Code-to-model traceability 56, Reproducibility package 54. Output judged: docs/media/coral_calice_septa_insertion_comparison.png: rendered output of 2013-thomas-coral-calice-septa-insertion.py at HEAD, image/png, 529340 B, 1495×1235 px, artifact_sha256 78be82bf5573c83c86c2ffc4b604d12fed23d472826afae1554dd32bee919d17 (sha256 78be82bf5573c83c86c2ffc4b604d12fed23d472826afae1554dd32bee919d17), spec_fingerprint 838f1452734ffec4b95f30098de1ca90f5c6e961cce22175354f682fa6865b61. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 838f1452734ffec4b95f30098de1ca90f5c6e961cce22175354f682fa6865b61; artifact_sha256: 78be82bf5573c83c86c2ffc4b604d12fed23d472826afae1554dd32bee919d17; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/coral_calice_septa_insertion_reference.json=9984d41d12285bd0..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/scleractinian_coral_septa_specimen.jpg=904035c936843361..., datasets/coral_calice_septa_insertion/scout_manifest.json=325761c7cb0d58db...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add runtime SHA-256 verification of all 4 dataset files, 7-species cross-taxa Scleractinian corallite scaling, 9 reference-anchored morphometrics in `measure_morphoeval()`, and an 8-check `self_test()` suite.",
        "remediation needed: Implement Chindapol et al. (2013) PLoS Comput. Biol. Péclet advection-diffusion boundary-layer solver across Pe in {0, 1, 4, 16, 36}, including the Pe = 0 hydrostatic pure-diffusion radial symmetry control and upstream-enhanced calcification flux.",
        "remediation needed: Implement Kunth's Law (1869) Paleozoic Rugosa serial 4-fossula septal insertion (N_rugosa(m) = 6 + 4m with cardinal/counter/alar pinnate bilateral symmetry) alongside Milne-Edwards hexameral cyclic doubling (N_hex(k) = 6 * 2^(k-1)) to demonstrate the evolutionary symmetry divergence proved in Lean 4 Theorem 2.",
        "remediation needed: Implement automated polar-coordinate ridge segmentation (`segment_caryophyllia_specimen`) on `scleractinian_coral_septa_specimen.jpg` to detect the 40 radiating septa (9.0 deg spacing) and quantify major (S1+S2) vs minor (S3+S4) radial reach ratios." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.18e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

